  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nNo significant weather impacts are expected over the next week\nplus. The pattern will continue to be dry with high pressure\ndominating for the bulk of the forecast period. Only exceptions\nwill be tomorrow afternoon and evening and again on Thursday as\ndry cold fronts push through the region. These fronts will bring\nan increase in wind gusts, however they will also bring an\nincrease in relative humidity, which alleviates some of our fire\nweather concerns. Wind gusts of 15 to 20 mph will be possible\nstarting tomorrow afternoon. Minimum RH will range in the upper\n40s to low 50s percent in the mid afternoon, before increasing\nin the late afternoon and evening as the stronger wind gusts\narrive. Due to the increase in RH, we are not expecting to issue\nany fire related special weather statements, but will continue\nto monitor fire weather conditions closely.",
